# Backend's Docker build context is the repo root (see
# docker/Dockerfile.backend's header comment for why), but this file lives
# here in docker/ rather than at the repo root -- BuildKit looks for a
# <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile it's building and
# uses that instead of a root-level .dockerignore when present (Docker
# 19.03+/BuildKit; docker/docker-compose.yml builds with BuildKit by
# default). Patterns below are still evaluated relative to the build
# context root (the repo root), not this directory. Without this file,
# the build would ship .git, every package's venv, node_modules, and local
# runtime data into the build context on every build.

.git
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
data/
backend/data/
ml/data/
frontend/.next
frontend/out
*.log
.env
**/.env
!**/.env.example
